{"role":"assistant","content":"The diagnosis is confirmed. In `bot.py:130-133`, `build_system()` concatenates the static `INSTRUCTIONS` with the per-athlete tail (which includes `facts`) into a **single** text block with one `cache_control` marker. Since Anthropic's prompt cache is a prefix hash, every `save_fact` appends a fact, changes the block, and evicts the whole prompt — the logs show exactly that: every round after a `save_fact` has `cache_read_input_tokens: 0` and `cache_creation_input_tokens` back up at ~1000+.\n\nThe fix, straight from the colleague's note: split `system` into two blocks with separate `cache_control: ephemeral` markers — static instructions first, volatile tail second. Applying it now:","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_RW5gGhLlTnzDn2A5TuIo7KoX","function":{"name":"Edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"bot.py\",\"old_string\":\"def build_system(a, today):\\n    # One block, cached as a whole: instructions + per-athlete context.\\n    text = INSTRUCTIONS + \\\"\\\\n\\\\n\\\" + athlete_context(a, today)\\n    return [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"text\\\": text, \\\"cache_control\\\": {\\\"type\\\": \\\"ephemeral\\\"}}]\",\"new_string\":\"def build_system(a, today):\\n    # Two cache breakpoints: the static instructions stay cached when a\\n    # memory write changes the per-athlete tail.\\n    return [\\n        {\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"text\\\": INSTRUCTIONS + \\\"\\\\n\\\\n\\\", \\\"cache_control\\\": {\\\"type\\\": \\\"ephemeral\\\"}},\\n        {\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"text\\\": athlete_context(a, today), \\\"cache_control\\\": {\\\"type\\\": \\\"ephemeral\\\"}},\\n    ]\"}"}}]}
